From: Tai Ci maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Do not patch jump offsets into a failed resolve_labels buffer

resolve_labels() records relocation addresses from bc_out.size while it
emits the optimized byte code. When growing bc_out fails, DynBuf keeps its
error flag and possibly a NULL buffer, but the label, jump shortening and
offset patching code still wrote through bc_out.buf (SIGSEGV in put_u8).
The writes are now skipped once bc_out is in error; the function already
reports out of memory after the loop.

Upstream quickjs-ng df836d1 contains the defect.
Found by Tai's loader-thread allocation failure sweep (tabset_loader_oom)
once the frozen runtime.js was embedded.
---
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -35857,7 +35857,9 @@
                 for(re = ls->first_reloc; re != NULL; re = re_next) {
                     int diff = ls->addr - re->addr;
                     re_next = re->next;
-                    switch (re->size) {
+                    /* after an allocation failure the addresses may lie
+                       outside the buffer; the function fails below */
+                    switch (dbuf_error(&bc_out) ? 0 : re->size) {
                     case 4:
                         put_u32(bc_out.buf + re->addr, diff);
                         break;
@@ -36553,7 +36555,8 @@
 
     /* more jump optimizations */
     patch_offsets = 0;
-    for (i = 0, jp = s->jump_slots; i < s->jump_count; i++, jp++) {
+    for (i = 0, jp = s->jump_slots;
+         !dbuf_error(&bc_out) && i < s->jump_count; i++, jp++) {
         LabelSlot *ls;
         JumpSlot *jp1;
         int j, pos, diff, delta;
@@ -36607,7 +36610,7 @@
         }
     }
 
-    if (patch_offsets) {
+    if (patch_offsets && !dbuf_error(&bc_out)) {
         JumpSlot *jp1;
         int j;
         for (j = 0, jp1 = s->jump_slots; j < s->jump_count; j++, jp1++) {
